tests
# …except the fixtures, which the build itself needs.
#
# scripts/check-standalone.mjs runs as postbuild and decodes a real HEIC with
# the copies of the decoders that are in .next/standalone. Excluding the whole
# tests directory meant the file was absent inside the image build, so the check
# reported it missing and failed — and the Docker build with it. Every deploy
# stopped, and the recovery endpoint could not reach production because no image
# carrying it was ever produced.
#
# The right fix is to carry the fixture rather than to soften the check. The
# Docker build is the artefact that gets deployed; a check that cannot run there
# is a check that does not run where it matters. It costs 718 KB in the build
# stage and nothing in the runtime image, which copies only .next/standalone.
!tests/fixtures
!tests/fixtures/**
*.md
!README.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
